# Per-run scratch fragments only.
.parity/

# parity.json is NOT ignored here any more. Under the old design the score was
# written back into the library repo it audited, so a copy under parity/ was a
# stray artifact. Under the cross-language harness (see HARNESS.md) each
# parity/<lib>/parity.json is regenerated by `go test` and IS the deliverable —
# the committed score for that library — so it has to be tracked.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Upstream oracle installs and build output.
#
# Every harness installs a real upstream library to compare against, and those
# trees are enormous — ~570 MB across the suite (streamlit's venv alone is
# 369 MB, prisma's node_modules 90 MB, sled's Rust target 47 MB). They are fully
# reproducible from the committed pins, so none of it belongs in git.
#
# What IS tracked, deliberately: the lockfiles that make the oracle
# reproducible — package.json/package-lock.json, requirements.txt, Cargo.toml/
# Cargo.lock, pom.xml, mix.exs/mix.lock, Gemfile/Gemfile.lock. An unpinned
# oracle makes a parity score meaningless, so never ignore those.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# node
node_modules/

# python
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# java / maven
target/

# elixir / mix
_build/
deps/

# ruby / bundler
# NB: the `**/` prefix is required. A pattern containing an interior slash is
# anchored to this .gitignore's own directory, so a bare `vendor/bundle/` would
# only match parity/vendor/bundle/ and would miss
# parity/migrate/ruby/vendor/bundle/ — which is 32 MB of compiled gems.
.bundle/
**/vendor/bundle/

# databases and images produced while running cases
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
out/
